YANI: Red specs.

I suggest the addition of two new items. Both would be described as
"red-tinted lenses" until IDed.

The first would be IDed as "infra-red goggles", which allow you to see
heat-producing monsters (ie anything but undead, ice-beasties, demons,
various other exceptions that ppl think of) and traps (fire-traps,
lava) anywhere on the current level. Maybe blessed they could help you
ID wands/ scrolls of fire as well.

The second item would ID as "rose-tinted spectacles", and they would
give all the usual spectacle benefits (improved searching, reading,
protection from blinding), but have a major drawback: When looking
through these any negative messages (ie messages about you getting
stabbed, beaten, bitten, eaten, set on fire, trapped, cursed, stoned,
frozen, crushed, level drained, having your intrinsics removed, your
inventory stolen and your pets killed etc) disappear completely.
Alternatively/ additionally, perhaps they could make all monsters- no
matter how big, scary and potentially lethal- appear as cute,
friendly, relatively harmless ickle fluffy things- kind of a
hallucination effect, I suppose, leading to great messages like "The
peaceful grid bug breathes a disintegration blast" and "The lichen
uses the finger of death", thus inducing the player to start attacking
pets and friendlies. Oh, rose-tinted specs would either make all traps
invisible or appear as fountains, altars and sinks, and they would
auto-curse, natuarally.

Combined with last year's YANI thread for cool dark sunglasses,
auto-tinting lenses and the "danger-sensitive" shades from HHGTTG I
think we have the makings of a complete "optician" patch.

